  <h2 id="faqs">FAQs</h2>
  <h3>Can you blackout after only a few drinks?</h3>
  <p>Yes. Drinking quickly, drinking on an empty stomach, certain medications, body size, and genetics can all contribute.</p>
  <h3>Do alcohol blackouts cause permanent brain damage?</h3>
  <p>Occasional blackouts usually do not, but repeated episodes are associated with long-term cognitive impairment.</p>
  <h3>Is having one blackout a sign of alcoholism?</h3>
  <p>Not necessarily. However, repeated blackouts are an important warning sign and should be evaluated by a healthcare professional.</p>
  <h3>Can you recover memories from a blackout?</h3>
  <p>Sometimes fragments return when the person is reminded by others, but complete blackouts often involve memories that were never stored in the brain.</p>

